  "id": "3455e8a0-28f3-5efa-97e0-675f8c6bc5b4",
  "slug": "real-homemade-tamales",
  "name": "Real Homemade Tamales",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This real homemade tamales recipe features tender pork mixed with a savory red chile sauce, wrapped in masa and corn husks, then steamed to perfection.",
  "cuisine": "Mexican Inspired Mexican",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Place pork, onion, and garlic in a Dutch oven. Add enough water to cover; bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Reduce the heat to low; simmer pork until cooked through and tender, about 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Remove stems and seeds from chiles; transfer to a medium saucepan with 2 cups water. Simmer, uncovered, for 20 minutes. Remove from heat to cool."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Transfer chiles and cooking liquid to a blender; blend until smooth. Strain sauce through a fine-mesh sieve into a bowl; stir in salt. Discard contents of strainer."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Remove pork from the pot; discard onion and garlic. Shred pork using two forks; mix in 1 cup chile sauce; set filling aside. Reserve remaining chile sauce for serving."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Soak corn husks in a bowl of warm water until softened, about 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Meanwhile, beat 1 tablespoon broth with lard in a large bowl until fluffy."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Combine masa harina, baking powder, and salt in another large bowl; stir into lard mixture, adding more broth as needed to form a soft, spongy dough."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Remove husks from water; pat dry. Spread about 2 tablespoons of dough, about 1/4-inch thick, onto the center of each husk, leaving a 1-inch border on sides and top."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Spoon 1 tablespoon pork filling over dough. Fold sides of husk toward the center, then fold up the bottom to seal. Repeat with remaining husks, dough, and filling."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "Arrange tamales upright in a steamer basket over simmering water. Cover with a damp towel or extra husks. Steam until dough is firm and pulls away easily from husks, about 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "text": "Unwrap the tamales; drizzle with remaining chile sauce. Top with sour cream. Alternatively, stir chile sauce and sour cream together before drizzling for a creamy option."
    }
  ],
